219: ### Where the threads end
220: 
221: Grade 12 is the subject's last year, and its rows hand on nothing. The research-cycle thread ends in the capstone
222: (g12-capstone-decision, unit 8), put to use on a real decision and published for the people it affects; the
223: search-plan and lateral-reading threads end in the personal system (g12-personal-system, unit 7), the student's own
224: way to find and check information after school; the lateral-reading thread's last classroom use is the capstone audit
225: (g12-lateral-capstone, unit 8); the citation thread ends in the capstone's method note and audit; honest use ends in
226: the student teaching it to someone younger (g12-help-others, unit 7). Beside library, ELA grade 12's senior research
227: project and US History II's researched argument use the same moves in their own courses.
