255: | 1, grade 9 mid-year | 1 | 1 | 1 | Day 8, week 15 of grade 9. Unit 1's end-of-unit assessment, one sitting of unseen invented items answered alone in writing (about 35 minutes): a too-broad question rewritten into a researchable one and the next round planned from a given log (g9-research-question-design); a search string with operators, truncation and two filters written for a new question (g9-databases-operators); the lateral routine run without the card on an unseen polished page (g9-lateral-method); a given log rechecked after a new finding, a source kept and one dropped with reasons (g9-source-log). The student's own revised log (unit 1, days 5 to 7) is scored as the I.D.2 product. As the band's first check it samples no earlier unit. The respond day (day 9, week 16) regroups by the rubric step missed and ends with one fresh try |
256: | 2, grade 9 year-end | 2 | 1 | 1 | Day 17, week 31 of grade 9. Unit 2's end-of-unit assessment, one sitting of unseen items: a one-sided paragraph rewritten to show two views at their strongest (g9-fair-sides); what three labeled works allow, and a permission request for one that does not (g9-open-licenses); the four fair use questions weighed on an unseen remix case, without a verdict of lawful (g9-open-licenses); from the student's own memo, how the group's findings changed their first idea (g9-group-shapes-solution, scored from unit 2's memo, day 16). It samples unit 1 on new cases: one lateral check of an unseen page and one operator string. The respond day (day 18, week 32) reteaches the gaps and closes the grade 9 year with a reflect step (the strongest step and one goal for grade 10) |
257: | 3, grade 10 mid-year | 3 | 1 | 1 | Day 26, week 15 of grade 10. Unit 3's end-of-unit assessment: on an unseen topic, how a reader's starting point could shape the reading, written about an invented reader or about oneself as the student chooses (g10-own-lens); subject terms and one reference followed back and one forward on an unseen database page, with an open-access copy found (g10-database-deep); a missing perspective named for a given source set, with where to find it and why it was missing (g10-others-views-in). Scored from unit 3's records: the seminar record sheet (day 24) and the log's missing-view line (day 23). It samples units 1 and 2 on new cases: one source log recheck and one license reading. The respond day (day 27, week 16) regroups by step missed |
